{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"The derivative can be found using **the power rule**:\n\n$\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x^n)=n\\cdot x^{n-1}$\n\n(Remember that this applies even when $n$ is a fraction.)","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(x^{^{\\Large\\frac{5}{3}}}\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{5}{3}x^{^{\\Large\\frac{5}{3}-1}}\\qquad\\gray{\\text{The power rule}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac53x^{^{\\Large\\frac{2}{3}}}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, we found that $\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(x^{^{\\Large\\frac{5}{3}}}\\right)=\\dfrac53x^{^{\\Large\\frac{2}{3}}}$.\n\nThis can also be written as ${\\dfrac53}{\\sqrt[3]{x^2}}$ (all equivalent forms are accepted).","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"$\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(x^{^{\\scriptsize\\dfrac{5}{3}}}\\right)=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"\\frac{5}{3}x^{\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)}"}],"buttonSets":["basic","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
